    <item>
      <title>Optimal regression design: an introduction</title>
      <link>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/opt_design/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/opt_design/</guid>
      <description>&lt;style&gt;&#xA;#resource-body table {&#xA;  display: block;&#xA;  max-width: 100%;&#xA;  overflow-x: auto;&#xA;  border-collapse: collapse;&#xA;  margin: 0.75rem 0;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body th, #resource-body td {&#xA;  padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem;&#xA;  vertical-align: top;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold {&#xA;  margin: 0.75rem 0;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary {&#xA;  display: list-item;&#xA;  list-style-position: inside;&#xA;  cursor: pointer;&#xA;  font-weight: 600;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary:focus-visible {&#xA;  outline: 2px solid currentColor;&#xA;  outline-offset: 4px;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold pre {&#xA;  margin-top: 0.5rem;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .design-illustration {&#xA;  margin: 1.1rem 0 1.4rem;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .design-illustration &gt; a {&#xA;  display: block;&#xA;  border-radius: 12px;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .design-illustration img {&#xA;  display: block;&#xA;  width: 100%;&#xA;  height: auto;&#xA;  border-radius: 12px;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .design-illustration figcaption {&#xA;  margin-top: 0.5rem;&#xA;  font-size: 0.9em;&#xA;  line-height: 1.5;&#xA;}&#xA;#resource-body .illustration-credit {&#xA;  display: block;&#xA;  margin-top: 0.2rem;&#xA;  font-size: 0.85em;&#xA;  opacity: 0.75;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Which experimental settings should we use, and how often should we repeat each one?&lt;/strong&gt; Optimal regression design answers this question by connecting a scientific goal to a statistical model and a limited experimental budget. The settings might be concentrations, sampling times, temperatures, or pool sizes. The goal might be precise parameter estimation, reliable response prediction, or learning a particular contrast.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>RAG systems: evidence, evaluation, and uncertainty</title>
      <link>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/rag_system/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/rag_system/</guid>
      <description>&lt;style&gt;&#xA;#resource-body table { display: block; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.75rem 0; }&#xA;#resource-body th, #resource-body td { padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; vertical-align: top; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold { margin: 0.75rem 0; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary { display: list-item; list-style-position: inside; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 4px; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold pre { margin-top: 0.5rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold { margin: 0.75rem 0 1.2rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; summary { display: list-item; list-style-position: inside; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 4px; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; ul, #resource-body .text-fold &gt; ol { margin-top: 0.65rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration { margin: 1.1rem 0 1.4rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration--plan { max-width: 560px; margin-inline: auto; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration &gt; a { display: block; border-radius: 12px; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration figcaption { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.5; }&#xA;#resource-body .illustration-credit { display: block; margin-top: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.85em; opacity: 0.75; }&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A useful research assistant should show where its answer comes from—and recognize when the available evidence is not enough.&lt;/strong&gt; Retrieval-augmented generation (&lt;strong&gt;RAG&lt;/strong&gt;) connects a language model to an external collection of documents. Instead of answering only from information encoded in its parameters, the model receives retrieved passages as context for its response. Lewis et al. introduced a prominent framework combining a neural retriever with a generative model. &lt;a href=&#34;#ref-rag&#34;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Drug discovery: statistics and AI agents</title>
      <link>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/drug_discovery/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/drug_discovery/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Drug discovery connects biological understanding with evidence about candidate compounds, including activity, toxicity, and how compounds behave in the body. These early investigations precede later stages of drug development. &lt;a href=&#34;#ref-fda&#34;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt; A statistical question runs through this process: &lt;strong&gt;which candidate or experiment should we investigate next, given limited data and resources?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The examples below introduce prediction, experiment selection, and uncertainty calibration, then show how an AI agent could connect them.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;model-the-response-and-its-uncertainty&#34; class=&#34;section level1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1&gt;1. Model the response and its uncertainty&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let &lt;span class=&#34;math inline&#34;&gt;\(x_i\)&lt;/span&gt; describe a candidate or experimental condition and &lt;span class=&#34;math inline&#34;&gt;\(y_i\)&lt;/span&gt; be its measured response. A simple working model is&lt;/p&gt;</description>
